/* Explore carousel status, beside the reading's time. dru's own vocabulary for
   all three banded metrics is VERY_LOW / LOW / NORMAL / ELEVATED / VERY_HIGH
   (`constants.ts`: glucose_range_text, blood_pressure_range_text,
   hba1c_range_text) — it has no "high" band, which is why the orange one is
   "elevated" (QA, 2026-09-08). Three words only: blood pressure's extra
   (yellow) band shares "elevated" with the orange one, and the colour is what
   distinguishes them. Arabic is the KSA table's own pairing, "elevated" =
   مرتفع. */
"normal" = "طبيعي";
"elevated" = "مرتفع";
"very high" = "مرتفع جداً";
/* The step goal on the Explore card — "goal" = الهدف in the KSA table. */
"goal" = "الهدف";
"Distance needs motion access" = "تتبع المسافة يحتاج إذن الحركة";

/* MARK: - Metric names
   The catalogue's `name_ar` differs per environment (dev says الرياضة for
   Workout, staging تمرين), so these are the approved words and the catalogue is
   the fallback — see `HealthSubcategory.displayName`. Keyed by the metric's
   English name, which is why they carry a prefix: the bare words are also units
